=== KVM/VM AGENT HANDBOOK: RED OS 8 CLI ===

1. VM METADATA
- VM Name (virsh): redos-mephi
- Guest Hostname: mephi-2026.domain.local
- OS: RED OS 8 Server (FSTEC, No GUI, RPM-based)
- Specs: 1 vCPU, 1536 MB RAM
- Storage (qcow2):
  * /var/lib/libvirt/images/redos-root.qcow2 -> mapped to /dev/vda (15G, OS)
  * /var/lib/libvirt/images/redos-data.qcow2 -> mapped to /dev/vdb (5G, Projects)

2. HOST CLI MANAGEMENT (Run on Ubuntu Host)
- Check status: sudo virsh list --all
- Boot VM:      sudo virsh start redos-mephi
- Shutdown VM:  sudo virsh shutdown redos-mephi
- Kill/Stop VM: sudo virsh destroy redos-mephi
- Toggle Boot:  sudo virsh autostart redos-mephi [--disable]

3. CONSOLE INTERACTION
- Connect to CLI: sudo virsh console redos-mephi
  *Note: Press [ENTER] after running to view login prompt.*
- Disconnect Escape Hotkey: Ctrl + ]
  *Note: Keeps VM alive in background.*

4. NETWORK DETAILS
- Mode: NAT via libvirt default network (192.168.122.0/24)
- Guest IP Discovery (from host): sudo virsh domifaddr redos-mephi
